35,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The management office charges 4,200 yen per hour, billed to one person. The spray receipts show 2,300 yen monthly, with significant duplicate purchases.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The timing is brutal: forty-seven minutes for the kitchen alone. With two people absent most months, the load concentrates on the remaining three. I need to know if outsourcing removes this entirely.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"My findings confirm the friction. ""Done"" is subjective, and every conflict started with a reminder. We’re not failing at cleaning; we’re failing at communication.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,"@Ryuji, forty-seven minutes is brutal! But my kitchen watch shows only two or three of us actually cook. The rest just make coffee. Why are we all cleaning up their mess?","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Midori,,"@Benjamin, the previous tenants divided rooms permanently, but by year two, two barely spoke. I’m worried we’ll end up in that silence. How do we keep talking?","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Ryuji, outsourcing at 4,200 yen an hour is expensive. But if it removes the duplicate spray purchases and the billing headache, it might be worth it.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Toshio, outsourcing removes the hours, but does it remove the coordination? If the firm arrives when I’m working, I lose the day. I need to know their scheduling terms.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Ryuji, coordination is the real cost. If the firm arrives when you’re working, you’ve just traded scrubbing for waiting. I need to see their scheduling terms.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"@Benjamin, coordination is key! But my watch shows the mess comes from just a few cooks. Why should coffee-drinkers pay for their mess?","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@May, I hear you. But if we split by usage, we might stop talking. I want a system where we check in, so the silence doesn’t turn into resentment.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@May, splitting by usage is administratively impossible. The management office bills one person, and the receipts show we waste money on duplicates. We need a single, predictable monthly figure.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Toshio, a single figure is fine, but the calendar shows two of us gone weekly. If the firm requires a keyholder, that burden falls on the remaining three. I need to know if they can self-access.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Ryuji, self-access is the only logical solution. If the firm can’t enter without us, we’re just outsourcing the waiting. I need to see their standard terms.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
